Project Overview
The Reading Room is a Java-based application designed to manage user authentication and enable users to interact with an online bookstore. This application features a secure login and signup system, allowing users to access a personalized dashboard and view available books. The project also includes an admin dashboard for managing books and users, leveraging a graphical user interface built with JavaFX and a backend database for persistent data storage. Additionally, unit tests ensure key functionalities are reliable and accurate.

Technologies Used
Java - Core programming language used to build the application.
JavaFX - Used for building the graphical user interface, providing an interactive experience for users.
SQLite - A lightweight, embedded database to store user data and book information persistently.
JUnit - Framework used for writing and running unit tests, ensuring code reliability and correctness.
Maven - Dependency management and build automation tool, used to streamline project setup and manage dependencies.

Testing
This project includes unit tests focused on the User class, ensuring the reliability of core functionalities such as user authentication,
signup, and data validation. The tests validate proper handling of user credentials, including both standard users and admin accounts,
as well as email format validation. JUnit has been used as the testing framework to verify expected behaviors and identify potential
issues,supporting robust development practices.